[about]
Title=2 - Install and Launch
Intro=One want: the kit on this computer, and a first look around it. Running the setup program and its finish page, the folder a command-line user may choose instead, then the HomerDev dialog on Alt plus Control plus Shift plus D: its list of everything in the kit, a sample opened from it, and the tutorials. This walk assumes walk zero.
Setup=Windows 10 or later, 64-bit, a screen reader running, and HomerDev underscore setup dot e x e downloaded from the kit's latest release.
Homework=Install the kit, open the HomerDev dialog, and run the C sharp fruit basket from it.

[step]
Say=The want: the kit on this computer, and a first look around. I run the setup program I downloaded. Windows asks for permission, since it installs for everyone on the computer, and then the wizard opens.
Key=Enter
Hear=Setup - HomerDev, Welcome to the HomerDev Setup Wizard
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]
Say=Enter through the pages. The kit goes to C colon backslash Program Files backslash HomerDev, the standard place for programs. The last page is the one to read.
Key=Enter
Hear=Install Ollama 0.40.3 (runs the local AI model), check box, checked

[step]
Say=The finish page offers every tool any Homer program uses, each worded by what this computer already has: Install when it is missing, Update when it is old, Reinstall, unticked, when it is current. So Enter alone installs what is missing and updates what is old. Down Arrow hears each box.
Key=Down
Hear=Install Pandoc 3.6 (converts documents between formats), check box, checked

[step]
Say=I press Enter on Finish. Each ticked tool installs in turn, and then one box says what happened.
Key=Enter
Hear=HomerDev Setup Results, dialog
Hear=HomerDev 1.67.0 is installed. Ollama was updated from 0.40.2 to 0.40.3. Logs are kept in C colon backslash Users backslash Jamal backslash AppData backslash Local backslash HomerDev backslash logs.

[step]
Say=One choice for later. If you type commands a lot, you can unzip HomerDev dot zip into C colon backslash HomerDev instead: the paths are shorter to type, and the kit works the same in either place.
Key=
Hear=

[step]
Say=Now the dialog, from anywhere in Windows: Alt plus Control plus Shift plus D. D for development.
Key=Alt+Control+Shift+D
Hear=HomerDev 1.72.0, dialog
Hear=Kit contents, list box, Document: AGENTS, HomerDev is a development kit for building Windows programs, documents, books, databases, installers and spoken tutorials for people who use screen readers, 1 of 130

[step]
Say=A hundred and thirty items: documents, samples, skills, templates, scripts and shared code, by kind and then by name. Control plus J searches the list. I search for fruit.
Key=Control+J
Hear=Search, edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]
Say=I type fruit and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=Sample: FruitBasketCs, C sharp, one dialog: the smallest Homer program, a list you add to and take from. Open runs it., 23 of 130
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]
Say=Enter opens the item I am on. A document opens in the browser, a file opens in a window I read line by line, and a sample runs.
Key=Enter
Hear=Fruit Basket, the basket is empty
Hear=Fruit, edit

[step]
Say=The window title carries the state, and focus starts in the field, because typing a fruit is the first thing anybody does. I type apple and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=apple added, 1 fruit in the basket

[step]
Say=One fruit, not one fruits: the noun matches the count. F1 for help: every Homer dialog describes its own fields.
Key=F1
Hear=Help, Fields in this dialog, Fruit, type the name of a fruit

[step]
Say=I close the basket with Alt plus F4, and the HomerDev dialog is where I left it.
Key=Alt+F4
Hear=HomerDev 1.72.0, dialog
Hear=Kit contents, list box, Sample: FruitBasketCs, 23 of 130
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]
Say=Down Arrow from here reaches the other three baskets: the same program with several windows inside one, and both again in Python. They answer every key alike, because the behaviour lives in the kit, not in either program. Walk three compares them.
Key=Down
Hear=Sample: FruitBasketMdiCs, C sharp, several windows inside one: the same basket as a multiple-document program. Open runs it., 25 of 130
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]
Say=Tab moves to the buttons. Play tutorials opens these ten walks in the Homer Player, Inix explained and Layout by Code show how settings and dialogs are written, and Ask an AI answers questions about the kit, typed or spoken, from the AI on this computer or Claude Code. The setup program has already told your AI tools where the kit is; walk eight says more.
Key=Tab
Hear=Open, button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]
Say=What this walk taught. I name the step; the reader gives the key or the command.
Key=
Hear=

[step]
Say=Install the kit and the tools.
Key=
Hear=HomerDev underscore setup dot e x e

[step]
Say=Open the HomerDev dialog.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Control plus Shift plus D

[step]
Say=Search the kit's contents.
Key=
Hear=Control plus J
